                <pb facs="0328" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg230"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1132/14: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jeffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-26T12:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 26,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 7 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>75. Department’s 44, October 23, 6 p.m. Am officially informed that President
                    Brum and the officials of the Government will be greatly pleased and feel highly
                    honored by visit from Secretary Colby. As the Uruguayan elections occur on
                    November 28th it is suggested the Secretary should not arrive at Montevideo on
                    this date nor Friday or Saturday preceding.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jeffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
